  "content": {
    "rendered": "<p>Are you wondering if you can change your child support order?</p>\n<p>Hi, I&#8217;m Marie Drake of The Drake Law Firm with offices in Golden and , and I&#8217;m going to talk to you today a little bit about what it takes to change a child support order.</p>\n<p>There’s several reasons why a court would grant a change in a child support order.</p>\n<p>One would be that the children&#8217;s needs have changed, another would be that, perhaps you&#8217;ve lost a job or your job has changed, and another one would be if there were additional children born, or if an older child goes away to college.</p>\n<p>These are changes where a court would grant a modification of your order.</p>\n<p>So if you&#8217;re thinking of changing a child support order, where do you start?</p>\n<p>What you need to do is file a motion to modify your current child support order, and in addition you&#8217;re going to have to update your financials with regard to income, so that the court can see and recalculate the support with some evidence behind it.</p>\n<p>Modifying child support can be tricky. There&#8217;s a process to follow, and you need to do that if you&#8217;re serious about this. So call an experienced family law attorney for some help.</p>\n<p>Here at The Drake Law Firm we&#8217;re standing by and we&#8217;re happy to help you, so give us a call.</p>\n<div class=\"ast-oembed-container \" style=\"height: 100%;\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Can You Change Your Child Support Order? | Child Custody Lawyers | The Drake Law Firm, P.C.\" width=\"500\" height=\"375\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/zD-Cl20jAA8?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>\n"
  },
